diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4a8ded5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Feature: Clear completed
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos
+  So that I can clean up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Clearing removes completed items
+
+    Scenario: Clicking clear-completed removes all completed todos
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: Clearing does not affect active items
+
+    Scenario: Active todos remain after clearing
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Clearing with mixed states
+
+    Scenario: Only completed items are removed
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog" and "Buy eggs"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is completed
+      When I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..db3498d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many items are left
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Counter shows active count
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero items left when no todos exist
+      Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows one item left
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows two items left
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Rule: Counter updates on completion
+
+    Scenario: Counter decrements when a todo is completed
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I complete the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter increments when a todo is uncompleted
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When I uncomplete the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Counter uses correct pluralization
+
+    Scenario: Singular form for one item
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Plural form for zero items
+      Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Plural form for multiple items
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Rule: Counter number is wrapped in strong tag
+
+    Scenario: The count number is bold
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter number is wrapped in a strong tag
diff --git a/features/editing.feature b/features/editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..779050a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct mistakes or update task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Save on Enter
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edited title
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I type "Buy eggs" in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I press Enter in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Buy eggs"
+      And the todo "Buy eggs" is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Save on blur
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edited title
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I type "Buy eggs" in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I blur the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs"
+
+  Rule: Empty edit destroys the todo
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I press Enter in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: Saving a whitespace-only edit removes the todo
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I type "   " in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I press Enter in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Escape discards changes
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape reverts to the original title
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I type "Buy eggs" in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I press Escape in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Edit input is trimmed
+
+    Scenario: Trailing and leading whitespace is removed from edits
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When I clear the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I type "  Buy eggs  " in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      And I press Enter in the edit input of "Buy milk"
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs"
diff --git a/features/item-interactions.feature b/features/item-interactions.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..37adfbd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/item-interactions.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Feature: Item interactions
+  As a user
+  I want to interact with individual todo items
+  So that I can complete, edit, or remove them
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Clicking the checkbox completes a todo
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle checkbox marks the todo as completed
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I click the checkbox of the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle checkbox again unmarks the todo
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I click the checkbox of the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not completed
+
+  Rule: Double-clicking a label activates editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters editing mode
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      And the edit input of "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Hovering shows the destroy button
+
+    Scenario: The destroy button is present on each todo
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has a destroy button
diff --git a/features/new-todo.feature b/features/new-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f96b797
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: New todo creation
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Empty or whitespace-only input is rejected
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter with an empty input creates no todo
+      When I press Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: Whitespace-only input is trimmed and rejected
+      When I type "   " in the new-todo input
+      And I press Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Valid input creates a todo
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter creates a todo from the input value
+      When I type "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+      And I press Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      When I type "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input
+      And I press Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: New todos are active by default
+
+    Scenario: A newly created todo is not completed
+      When I type "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+      And I press Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then the first todo is not completed
+
+  Rule: The new-todo input is focused on load
+
+    Scenario: The input has focus when the page loads
+      Then the new-todo input has focus
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2ae8f75
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Local storage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I don't lose my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Todos are saved to localStorage
+
+    Scenario: Added todos persist after page reload
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And I have added a todo "Walk the dog"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Completion state persists
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists after page reload
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Rule: Deleted todos stay deleted
+
+    Scenario: Destroyed todos do not reappear after reload
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I destroy the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: localStorage key format
+
+    Scenario: Todos are stored under the correct key
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then localStorage contains a key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Rule: Editing mode is not persisted
+
+    Scenario: A todo in editing mode is saved without editing class on reload
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
