+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on what matters
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all todos
+
+    Scenario: All todos are visible on the default route
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I navigate to "#/"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Rule: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+
+    Scenario: Completed todos are hidden on the active filter
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is hidden
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Rule: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+
+    Scenario: Active todos are hidden on the completed filter
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I navigate to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" is hidden
+
+  Rule: Filter links reflect current route
+
+    Scenario: The selected class is applied to the active filter link
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+      And the "All" filter link is not selected
+      And the "Completed" filter link is not selected
+
+  Rule: Items update when filtered
+
+    Scenario: Completing an item on the active filter hides it
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      And I complete the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is hidden
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Rule: Route persists on reload
+
+    Scenario: The active filter is maintained after page reload
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the "Active" filter link is selected
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c9446a5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want to toggle all todos at once
+  So that I can quickly mark everything done or undone
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all checks all todos
+
+    Scenario: Clicking toggle-all when all items are active marks all completed
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos are completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all unchecks all todos
+
+    Scenario: Clicking toggle-all when all items are completed marks all active
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos are not completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all reflects individual state
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all becomes checked when all items are individually completed
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When I complete the todo "Buy milk"
+      And I complete the todo "Walk the dog"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all becomes unchecked when any item is individually unchecked
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When I uncomplete the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all state is reset after clear completed
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all is unchecked after clearing completed items
+      Given I have added todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a075bc5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Section visibility
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show relevant sections only when needed
+  So that the interface stays clean
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+
+    Scenario: The main section is hidden when the todo list is empty
+      Then the main section is hidden
+
+    Scenario: The footer is hidden when the todo list is empty
+      Then the footer is hidden
+
+  Rule: Main and footer appear when todos exist
+
+    Scenario: The main section is visible when a todo is added
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the main section is visible
+
+    Scenario: The footer is visible when a todo is added
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the footer is visible
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button visibility
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button hides after all completed are cleared
+      Given I have added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
